# Ignore-file scoped to CSharp/OpenTraceability.TestServer/Dockerfile.
#
# WHY THIS FILENAME: BuildKit looks for "<dockerfile-filename>.dockerignore" next to the Dockerfile
# before falling back to "<context-root>/.dockerignore". Naming it this way keeps these rules off
# every other image built from this repository - DiagnosticsTool builds from the same
# repository-root context and must keep seeing the whole tree. Requires BuildKit/buildx, which is
# what docker build, docker compose build and docker/build-push-action all use; under
# DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0 this file is not read and the whole repository is sent - slower, never wrong.
#
# WHY AN ALLOWLIST: the context is the repository root, because OpenTraceability.csproj embeds
# schema files through ..\..\docs\ links that must resolve to /docs. The root carries ~1.1 GB the
# image never needs (.git, Java/, .vs/, bin/obj of eight projects, a local epcis.db). Everything is
# denied first; only the TestServer's four-project build closure and the four embedded schema
# documents are re-included.
#
# PATTERN SEMANTICS - two rules that are easy to get wrong:
#  1. Patterns are relative to the BUILD CONTEXT ROOT, never to this folder. Hence every line
#     starts with CSharp/ or docs/.
#  2. Last match wins, so the re-exclusions must stay below the re-inclusions; and each
#     re-inclusion must spell out its parent path literally. A "!**/Foo" pattern would not work:
#     the walker prunes CSharp/ before it ever reaches Foo.
#
# IF THE BUILD FAILS with MSB3202 or a missing EmbeddedResource, a ProjectReference or docs/ file
# was added and must be re-included below. DockerIgnoreClosureTests asserts this list stays in
# sync with the project graph and names what is missing.

# --- Deny everything ---------------------------------------------------------------------
**

# --- Re-include the TestServer build closure (4 of the 8 projects under CSharp/) -----------
# OpenTraceability.TestServer -> OpenTraceability.TestServerPackage -> OpenTraceability.GDST
#                             -> OpenTraceability (leaf)
!CSharp/OpenTraceability/**
!CSharp/OpenTraceability.GDST/**
!CSharp/OpenTraceability.TestServerPackage/**
!CSharp/OpenTraceability.TestServer/**

# Repository-wide MSBuild/NuGet configuration. None of these exist today; they are listed so that
# adding one later changes the container build the same way it changes a local build, instead of
# silently applying only outside Docker.
!global.json
!NuGet.config
!nuget.config
!Directory.Build.props
!Directory.Build.targets
!Directory.Packages.props
!.editorconfig
!CSharp/global.json
!CSharp/NuGet.config
!CSharp/nuget.config
!CSharp/Directory.Build.props
!CSharp/Directory.Build.targets
!CSharp/Directory.Packages.props
!CSharp/.editorconfig

# --- The four schema documents embedded by OpenTraceability.csproj -------------------------
!docs/epcis/epcis_schema.json
!docs/gdst/gdst_json_schema.json
!docs/gdst/gdst_openapi.yaml
!docs/beefleather/beefleather_openapi.yaml

# --- Re-exclude build, IDE and local artefacts inside the kept trees. Must stay last. ------
CSharp/**/bin
CSharp/**/obj
CSharp/**/.vs
CSharp/**/TestResults
CSharp/**/*.user
CSharp/**/*.suo
CSharp/**/*.lscache
CSharp/**/*.pubxml
CSharp/**/.DS_Store
CSharp/OpenTraceability.TestServer/Properties/PublishProfiles
CSharp/OpenTraceability.TestServer/Properties/ServiceDependencies
CSharp/**/launchSettings.json

# Local SQLite database left behind by running the server outside Docker (~7 MB with -wal/-shm).
CSharp/**/*.db
CSharp/**/*.db-shm
CSharp/**/*.db-wal

# Developer-only configuration. Keeping it out of the context keeps it out of the published image;
# see the "Docker build context" section of README.md for the BaseURL behaviour this changes.
CSharp/**/appsettings.Development.json

# Package readme files. They are packed into the nupkgs straight from source and are never an input
# to a build, so they have no business in the image.
CSharp/**/*.md

# The Dockerfile and this file are read by the client from disk, not from the transferred context,
# so excluding them changes nothing except keeping them out of /src.
CSharp/**/Dockerfile*
